# #1898: verify-proposal-refs.sh and tests/test-verify-proposal-refs.sh carry
# a fix for a SIGPIPE race under `set -o pipefail` and a subshell-in-pipe cache
# bug (closing #1863 via PR #1881), both issues that produced flaky false
# "MISSING FILE" reports on paths that actually exist, especially early-sorting
# paths like `docs/...` entries. The fix replaces a `full_tree()` helper
# function and `full_tree | grep -qFx` pipe with a direct `FULL_TREE_CACHE`
# assignment and here-string match (`grep -qFx "$path" <<< "$FULL_TREE_CACHE"`),
# and restores `Fixture 5b` (8-iteration flake-detection loop) to the test suite.
# A same-day resync commit (fcbf52f8, 2026-09-15T17:03:12Z) reverted both halves
# of that fix back to the buggy pre-#1881 state, so this pin prevents an
# unlimited stream of recurrences of the same reversion pattern as #606/#662/
# #1292/#1316/#1356/#1546/#1674. This fix was never upstreamed into
# rjwalters/loom's own templates, so an unpinned resync would keep reverting it.
# If the upstream Loom project ever adopts an equivalent SIGPIPE race fix and
# flake-detection test, this pin can be dropped and the files resynced normally.
scripts/verify-proposal-refs.sh
scripts/tests/test-verify-proposal-refs.sh

# #2020: pr-worktree.sh carries a local-only call to the repo-owned
# .loom/hooks/post-worktree.sh (a `run_post_worktree_hook` helper, invoked
# both from the "reuse an existing PR worktree" path and the "freshly
# created PR worktree" path) so a PR review worktree gets its own uv-synced
# venv + editable install, the same treatment worktree.sh already gave issue
# worktrees. Without it, `pytest` run inside a `.loom/worktrees/pr-<N>/`
# review worktree could silently import the MAIN CHECKOUT's src/ via a stale
# editable install recorded elsewhere -- a false negative on a PR that fixes
# a bug (old code still runs) or a false positive on a PR that introduces
# one (discovered evaluating PR #2013, reproduced in
# `.loom/worktrees/pr-2013`). This call was never upstreamed into
# rjwalters/loom's own pr-worktree.sh template (klayout-tools is a uv-based
# Python project; upstream's own template has no Python-specific setup
# step), so an unpinned resync would silently drop it -- the same reversion
# pattern as #606/#662/#1292/#1316/#1356/#1546/#1674/#1898. If the upstream
# Loom project ever adopts an equivalent post-worktree-hook call from
# pr-worktree.sh, this pin can be dropped and the file resynced normally.
scripts/pr-worktree.sh

# #2193: check-promotion-landed.sh (and its test) carry a local-only "Step 1c"
# guard that treats a current `loom:operator-only` label exactly like the
# `loom:building`/`loom:blocked` labels its Step 1b later-lifecycle guard
# already recognized -- DECISION=OK (or ALREADY_ESCALATED when this script's
# own `<!-- champion:promotion-landed-mismatch -->` marker comment shows a
# prior run raised the escalation), never a label write. Upstream's version
# checks `loom:operator-only` ONLY inside the tier-UNRECOVERABLE escalation
# branch, so an issue with a stale `Champion Review: APPROVED` comment, no
# `loom:issue`, and a recoverable tier took the DECISION=COMPLETED branch and
# re-applied `loom:issue` + tier on top of a live human escalation. Observed
# live on issue #1779 (2026-09-20): approved 2026-09-14, weeks of legitimate
# loom:blocked/loom:curated dependency cycling, correctly re-escalated to
# loom:operator-only,loom:operator-decision, then overwritten ~15 hours later
# by Pass 0c -- bypassing a pending human ruling, caught and reverted by hand
# before a Builder claimed it. This contradicts champion-issue-promo.md /
# champion-pr-merge.md's own "When NOT to Promote" rule (Champion must never
# write loom:issue onto a loom:operator-only issue). The fix was not upstreamed
# into rjwalters/loom's own check-promotion-landed.sh template, so an unpinned
# resync would silently revert it -- the same reversion pattern as
# #606/#662/#1292/#1316/#1356/#1546/#1674/#1898/#2020. If the upstream Loom
# project ever adopts an equivalent guard, these pins can be dropped and the
# files resynced normally.
scripts/check-promotion-landed.sh
scripts/tests/test-check-promotion-landed.sh
